>Anyone have a list of eating what creature does what? Also, if you
>eat monsters, does this extend the time you have to go between eating
>food rations? I've had enough characters starve to death....

	I don't have a list, but I can give you a few rules of thumb a
carnivore should keep in mind.

	1) With the exception of poison resistance, the abilities a monster
corpse can give you are usually intuitive based on the nature of the monster;
eating the corpse of a fire-breathing dragon has a good chance of making you
immune to fire.  Poison resistance is conferred by monsters that are immune to
poison.

	2) The food value of a monster corpse is proportional to its weight; a
newt corpse is barely a snack, while a dragon or giant corpse could keep you
stuffed for weeks.

	3) Unless you have some stong healing magic (extra healing, a unicorn
horn, or lots of brownie points with your god), stay away from corpses that
aren't particularly fresh.  If you happen to eat one that's too old, you will
be infected with a deadly disease.  If your dog won't touch it, you shouldn't
either.  Undead corpses are frequently rotten *before* you kill them.

	Bon appetit!

